# Pairs with ReadPositionHonest. A leaf whose snapshot vanished starts cold
# whenever the WAL's tail still reads 0. The pin store keeps the entitlement the
# vanished snapshot licensed, so the GC trims the prefix during the cold rebuild
# and the leaf reads past an owned write it never holds (the #4653 review's
# depth-18 trace). The base fails closed whatever the tail. Production analogue:
# #4653's perturbation M9, red on
# VanishedSnapshotColdStartIntegrationTests.A_cold_start_over_a_vanished_snapshot_fails_closed_even_when_the_tail_is_untrimmed_at_activation.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestVanishedSnapshotTailZeroShortcut
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a vanished snapshot starts cold while the tail reads 0, and the GC trims under the rebuild
PERTURBS: Activate

--- FIND
    /\ ~stale[l]
    /\ ~SnapshotVanished(l)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the cold start is allowed while nothing has been trimmed yet.
    /\ ~stale[l]
    /\ ~(SnapshotVanished(l) /\ tail > 0)
--- END
--- FIND
SnapshotLoss == FALSE
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the environment may destroy a snapshot.
SnapshotLoss == TRUE
--- END

--- FIND
MaxFaults == 1
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the snapshot vanishes and its leaf stops: two faults.
MaxFaults == 2
--- END